gartner-hypecycle-graph: 1
# A hand-authored hype cycle of electric vehicles, from the lead-acid battery to ideas that have not
# started yet. Dates after 2026 are projections, and dates and influences are illustrative, not a
# claim: see readme.md.
trends:
  - id: lead-acid-battery
    name: Lead-acid battery
    start: 1859-01
    stop: 1990-01
    row: 0
    phases: 4
    tags: [batteries]
    description: Gaston Planté's rechargeable cell of 1859, still the starter battery in most cars.
  - id: nickel-metal-hydride
    name: Nickel-metal hydride batteries
    start: 1989-01
    stop: 2015-01
    row: 2
    phases: 4
    tags: [batteries]
  - id: lithium-ion-batteries
    name: Lithium-ion batteries
    start: 1991-06
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 0
    phases: 4
    tags: [batteries]
  - id: lithium-iron-phosphate
    name: Lithium iron phosphate
    start: 1997-01
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 4
    phases: 3
    tags: [batteries]
    description: Cheaper, safer cells without cobalt, back in favour from 2021.
  - id: gigafactories
    name: Gigafactories
    start: 2014-02
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 6
    phases: 2
    tags: [batteries, industry]
  - id: solid-state-batteries
    name: Solid-state batteries
    start: 2017-01
    stop: 2034-01
    row: 2
    phases: 2
    tags: [batteries]
  - id: battery-recycling
    name: Battery recycling
    start: 2019-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 8
    phases: 1
    tags: [batteries, circular]
  - id: sodium-ion-batteries
    name: Sodium-ion batteries
    start: 2021-07
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 10
    phases: 1
    tags: [batteries]
    description: CATL's first sodium-ion cells of 2021, made without lithium.
  - id: early-electric-cars
    name: Early electric cars
    start: 1890-01
    stop: 1925-01
    row: 12
    phases: 2
    tags: [vehicles]
    description: Electric taxis in New York and London around 1900, beaten by the cheap petrol car.
  - id: zev-mandate
    name: Zero-emission mandate and the EV1
    start: 1990-09
    stop: 2003-12
    row: 14
    phases: 2
    tags: [vehicles, policy]
    description: California's mandate brought GM's EV1, which GM recalled and crushed in 2003.
  - id: hybrid-cars
    name: Hybrid cars
    start: 1997-12
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 12
    phases: 4
    tags: [vehicles]
    description: From the Toyota Prius of 1997.
  - id: fuel-cell-cars
    name: Fuel cell cars
    start: 2002-12
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 16
    phases: 2
    tags: [vehicles, hydrogen]
  - id: battery-electric-cars
    name: Battery electric cars
    start: 2008-02
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 18
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 2013-06
    trough-end: 2019-01
    tags: [vehicles]
    description: From the Tesla Roadster and the Nissan Leaf on.
  - id: ev-incentives
    name: EV incentives and bans
    start: 2009-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 14
    phases: 3
    tags: [policy]
    description: Tax credits, China's new-energy vehicle quota, and bans on new petrol cars from 2035.
  - id: electric-bikes-and-scooters
    name: Electric bikes and scooters
    start: 2010-01
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 20
    phases: 3
    tags: [micromobility]
  - id: electric-buses
    name: Electric buses
    start: 2010-06
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 22
    phases: 3
    tags: [vehicles, transit]
    description: Shenzhen's whole bus fleet went electric by 2017.
  - id: electric-trucks
    name: Electric trucks
    start: 2017-11
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 26
    phases: 2
    tags: [vehicles, freight]
  - id: electric-air-taxis
    name: Electric air taxis
    start: 2016-09
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 24
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2022-01
    tags: [aviation, upcoming]
    description: Electric vertical take-off aircraft; several makers went bankrupt before certification.
  - id: battery-swapping
    name: Battery swapping
    start: 2007-10
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 30
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 2013-05
    trough-end: 2020-01
    tags: [charging]
    description: Better Place went bankrupt in 2013; NIO revived the idea in China.
  - id: charging-standards
    name: Charging connector standards
    start: 2010-03
    stop: 2030-01
    row: 32
    phases: 3
    tags: [charging]
    description: From CHAdeMO and CCS to the North American standard most makers adopted in 2023.
  - id: vehicle-to-grid
    name: Vehicle-to-grid
    start: 2012-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 34
    phases: 2
    tags: [charging, grid]
  - id: public-fast-charging
    name: Public fast charging
    start: 2012-09
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 38
    phases: 3
    tags: [charging]
    description: From Tesla's first Superchargers in 2012.
  - id: software-defined-vehicles
    name: Software-defined vehicles
    start: 2012-06
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 36
    phases: 2
    tags: [software]
    description: Cars updated over the air, from the Model S on.
  - id: self-driving
    name: Driver assistance and self-driving
    start: 2004-03
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 28
    phases: 3
    peak-end: 2018-03
    trough-end: 2023-06
    tags: [software, autonomy]
    description: From the DARPA Grand Challenge of 2004; the hype broke after the first fatal crash in 2018.
  - id: robotaxis
    name: Robotaxis
    start: 2020-10
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 40
    phases: 1
    tags: [autonomy, upcoming]
    description: Driverless rides for the public, from Waymo in Phoenix in 2020.
  - id: wireless-charging-roads
    name: Dynamic wireless charging roads
    start: 2028-01
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 42
    phases: 1
    tags: [charging, conceptual]
    description: Coils under the road that charge a car while it drives.
  - id: structural-batteries
    name: Structural batteries
    start: 2029-01
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 44
    phases: 1
    tags: [batteries, conceptual]
    description: Cells that are the car's body, carrying load and storing energy at once.
  - id: lithium-air-batteries
    name: Lithium-air batteries
    start: 2030-01
    stop: 2048-01
    row: 46
    phases: 1
    tags: [batteries, conceptual]
    description: Close to petrol's energy density on paper, far from it in the lab.
triggers:
  - id: prius-unveiled
    name: Toyota Prius unveiled
    date: 1997-10
    row: 11
    tags: [vehicles]
    description: The first mass-produced hybrid car was shown in Tokyo and went on sale in Japan that December.
  - id: tesla-roadster-unveiled
    name: Tesla Roadster unveiled
    date: 2006-07
    row: 17
    tags: [vehicles, batteries]
    description: A sports car running on thousands of laptop lithium-ion cells.
  - id: dieselgate
    name: Dieselgate
    date: 2015-09
    row: 13
    tags: [policy]
    description: Volkswagen admitted to cheating emissions tests, and the case for clean diesel collapsed.
  - id: model-3-deliveries
    name: Model 3 deliveries begin
    date: 2017-07
    row: 5
    tags: [vehicles]
    description: The first electric car built for the volume market by a company that made nothing else.
  - id: us-inflation-reduction-act
    name: US Inflation Reduction Act
    date: 2022-08
    row: 7
    tags: [policy]
    description: Tax credits tied to where batteries and their minerals are made.
  - id: eu-2035-agreement
    name: EU 2035 combustion-car deal
    date: 2022-10
    row: 13
    tags: [policy]
    description: The European Parliament and Council agreed that new cars sold from 2035 must emit no CO2.
